{ JSON in paslang (P202, P203): the json type's runtime, its words
  (JsonParse, JsonEncode, EJsonError, the members of TJsonHelper) and
  JSON's scans, one kernel per machine.

  A document is one block that holds no pointer: a header, a node of 16
  bytes for every value and every member's name in the order of the
  text, and an arena for the characters of the strings and the text of
  the numbers (docs/TYPES.md, json). A json is the address of a node, nil
  for null; nothing writes a document once parsed, so any number of
  routines read one at once. A parse checks the text is UTF-8 (passtr's
  kernel), runs the structural scan below over it to count what the
  document needs, reserves it once at that size and fills it as the
  scan runs again, a window of 64 KiB at a time, under a state machine
  with an explicit stack of the open containers (no recursion, so the
  10000 levels Go takes need no stack): Go's encoding/json/v2 strictness
  (jsontext/state.go, decode.go, jsonwire/decode.go) and its errors,
  their offsets, pointers and reasons as Go's SyntacticError gives them.
  The writer is Go's jsonwire (AppendQuote, AppendFloat, CompareUTF16)
  in two passes, the size and then the bytes. Plain, a parser that reads
  a byte at a time, is the one the tests hold the other to, block for
  block.

  The scans: the structural scan of a text, which the parser reads, and
  the escape finder of the writer. Go reads JSON a byte at a time
  (encoding/json/jsontext), so where it has no SIMD the scan follows
  simdjson 5.0.3's stage 1
  (docs/ref/json/simdjson-5.0.3, src/generic/stage1:
  json_escape_scanner.h, json_string_scanner.h, json_scanner.h,
  json_structural_indexer.h; the classification of src/haswell.cpp and
  src/arm64.cpp). Each kernel has a body on the processor's extension
  (Cpu), one on the base processor (Base) and the Pascal it does
  (Plain), which the tests hold them to.

  The scan reads 64 bytes a block. Each byte takes a class from two
  tables of 16, the one by its high four bits ANDed with the one by its
  low four: a comma, a colon, a bracket or a brace, a space, a tab, a
  line feed or a carriage return, a control byte, an opening bracket or
  brace. The class is exact for every byte, where simdjson's tables
  also take 0Ch and 1Ah (haswell) or FFh (arm64) for operators. A
  backslash that escapes is told from one that is escaped by the borrow
  of a subtraction over the odd bits (json_escape_scanner.h); a quote
  not escaped opens or closes a string, and a prefix XOR of the quotes,
  six shifts and XORs, says which bytes lie inside one.

  The index is the places, from the start of the text, of every quote;
  of every comma, colon, bracket and brace outside a string and of the
  first byte of every other scalar there; and of every escaping
  backslash and every control byte inside a string. The parser finds
  each value there, and each string's end and escapes without reading
  its bytes again, and a control byte in a string, an error, at its
  place. The scan also counts what the document needs: its values and
  member names (Nodes), its scalars that are not strings (Scalars), and
  the bytes of its strings from their opening quote and of its other
  scalars (Bytes), so that the parser reserves the document once, at
  its size.

  amd64 AVX2 with BMI1 and POPCNT, the build for x86-64-v3: VPSHUFB
  looks the tables up, VPCMPEQB and VPMOVMSKB make the masks, ANDN and
  POPCNT work on them, TZCNT and BLSR write the index eight places a
  step. SSE2 on the base processor: PCMPEQB for each character, the
  bits counted by halves (SWAR), BSF. arm64 NEON, part of the base
  processor: TBL for the tables, CMEQ and CMTST, each mask by the AND
  of every bit's weight and ADDP, CNT and UADDLP for the counts, RBIT
  once and CLZ for the index (simdjson's arm64 bit_indexer).

  The escape finder gives the first byte of a string that JSON writes
  escaped: a quote, a backslash, a control byte and, for HTML, the
  ampersand and the angle brackets. AVX2 and NEON look two tables up,
  SSE2 compares; each reads aligned blocks, which never cross a page,
  and drops what lies outside the string. }

unit pasjson;

interface

{ The json type's runtime (P203) is compiled by a paslangc that knows
  json, 1.1.124 and after; an older one, the host that builds the stage
  compiler (Regla 15), compiles the scans alone, which that compiler
  links. }
{$if PASLANG_FULLVERSION >= 1001124}
uses pasobject, pasnum, passtr, pasfmt, pasroutines;
{$endif}

type
  { The scan's state from one call to the next, and its counts (P202);
    PasJsonScanStart sets it for a new text. }
  TPasJsonScan = record
    Escaped: Int64;   { 1 when the next byte follows a backslash that escapes it }
    InStr: Int64;     { -1 when the last byte lies inside a string, else 0 }
    Scalar: Int64;    { 1 when the last byte belongs to a scalar that is not a string }
    Nodes: Int64;     { values and member names: strings, other scalars, opening brackets and braces }
    Scalars: Int64;   { scalars that are not strings }
    Bytes: Int64;     { bytes of the strings from their opening quote, and of the other scalars }
  end;

{$if PASLANG_FULLVERSION >= 1001124}
  { What a json value is (P203): null (nil is null too), true or
    false, a number, a string, an array, an object. }
  TJsonKind = (jkNull, jkBoolean, jkNumber, jkString, jkArray, jkObject);
  { Why a parse or a read failed: the text is no JSON (jeSyntax), not
    UTF-8 or holds a noncharacter (jeEncoding, RFC 7493 2.1), an object
    names a member twice (jeDuplicate), nests past MaxDepth (jeDepth) or
    is longer than MaxBytes (jeTooLarge); a read asked for a member
    that is not there (jeMissing), of a value of another kind (jeType)
    or for an element or a number past its range (jeRange); a decode met
    a member no field takes with RejectUnknown (jeUnknown, P206); a
    JsonPatch's test found another value (jeTest, P207); a stream's
    read or write failed or passed its deadline (jeIO, P208). }
  TJsonErrorKind = (jeSyntax, jeEncoding, jeDuplicate, jeDepth, jeTooLarge, jeMissing, jeType,
    jeRange, jeUnknown, jeTest, jeIO);

  { How a parse reads and how JsonEncode writes, one call at a time:
    nothing about JSON is global. JsonDefaults, JsonPretty and
    JsonCanonical give the usual ones. }
  TJsonOptions = record
    MaxDepth: Integer;     { the deepest nesting a parse takes: 10000 by default, as Go's }
    MaxBytes: Integer;     { the longest text a parse takes, 0 for any (at most 4 GiB - 1) }
    Indent: string;        { JsonEncode: '' on one line, else a value a line, Indent a level }
    Canonical: Boolean;    { JsonEncode: RFC 8785's form, which Indent does not change }
    EscapeHtml: Boolean;   { JsonEncode: <, > and & as \u003c, \u003e and \u0026 }
    RejectUnknown: Boolean; { JsonDecode: a member no field takes is an error, unless one is json unknown }
    Merge: Boolean;        { JsonDecode: into what is there, objects member by member, as Go's v2 }
  end;

  { The error of a parse or a read: where it is (Offset, the byte from
    0; Line and Column, from 1, the column in bytes; 0 for a read), the
    JSON Pointer of the value it is about (RFC 6901) and why. Like every
    raised object, it belongs to the routine that raised it. }
  EJsonError = class(TObject)
  private
    FKind: TJsonErrorKind;
    FOffset, FLine, FColumn: Integer;
    FPath, FReason, FMessage: string;
  public
    constructor Create(AKind: TJsonErrorKind; AOffset, ALine, AColumn: Integer;
      const APath, AWhere, AReason: string);
    function ToString: string; override;
    property Kind: TJsonErrorKind read FKind;
    property Offset: Integer read FOffset;
    property Line: Integer read FLine;
    property Column: Integer read FColumn;
    property Path: string read FPath;
    property Reason: string read FReason;
    property Message: string read FMessage;
  end;

  { for ... in a json: the next child and how many are left. }
  TJsonIter = record
    Cur: Pointer;      { the next element, or the next member's name }
    Left: Integer;
    Index: Integer;    { the next element's place }
    Obj: Boolean;
  end;

  { An object's members or an array's elements read in O(1) (P203): a
    table of the names, seeded per index (XxHash3 with a seed from the
    process's key, as an object's names are checked for twins), or the
    places of the elements. It never changes once made, so any number
    of routines read one at once, as the document. }
  TJsonIndex = class(TObject)
  private
    FDoc: json;
    FNames: array of Pointer;   { the name nodes, nil for a free slot }
    FMask: Integer;
    FSeed: Integer;
    FItems: array of Pointer;   { an array's elements }
  public
    constructor Create(J: json);
    function Get(const Name: string): json;
    function Find(const Name: string): json;
    function Has(const Name: string): Boolean;
    function Item(I: Integer): json;
    function Count: Integer;
    property Doc: json read FDoc;
  end;

  { A json's members and their reads. A document never changes, so any
    number of routines read one at once. A helper of a program's own
    for json hides this one unless it descends from it:
    type helper(TJsonHelper) for json. }
  TJsonHelper = type helper for json
    function Kind: TJsonKind;
    function IsNull: Boolean;
    function AsBoolean: Boolean;
    function AsInteger: Integer;
    function AsFloat: Double;
    function AsQuad: Quad;
    function AsCurrency: Currency;
    function AsString: string;
    function AsNumber: string;
    function At(const Ptr: string): json;
    function Find(const Name: string): json;
  end;

  { The writer of the encoders the compiler writes for a record, a class
    or any type JsonEncode takes (P205): the text, and a level for each
    open object or array, for its commas and for the JSON Pointer an
    error names. One routine owns a writer while it writes. }
  TJsonOutLevel = record
    Count: Integer;     { the members or elements written }
    Obj: Boolean;
    NameP: Pointer;     { the last member's name as it was written, "name": }
    NameN: Integer;
  end;
  TJsonOut = record
    S: string;          { the text, longer than what is written }
    N: Integer;         { the bytes written }
    Depth: Integer;     { the open objects and arrays }
    MaxDepth: Integer;
    ValAt: Integer;     { where the value of the last member begins }
    Indent: string;     { '' on one line }
    Pad: string;        { a line feed and Indent as many times as the deepest level so far }
    Html: Boolean;
    Lv: array of TJsonOutLevel;
  end;
  { where a member began, for omitempty to take it back }
  TJsonOutMark = record
    N, Count: Integer;
  end;
  { a map's keys and the names they are written as, ordered by name
    before its members are written }
  TJsonOutPair = record
    Name: string;
    Key: Integer;
  end;
  TJsonOutPairs = array of TJsonOutPair;
  { A typed decode's cursor (P206, P280): what its options ask, and the
    text it reads a token at a time, with no document, or the nodes of
    the json it reads. One routine owns it while it decodes. }
  TJsonIn = record
    Merge: Boolean;     { into what is there, as Go's v2 unmarshals }
    Reject: Boolean;    { a member no field takes is an error }
    Text: string;       { the text read, '' for a json }
    Opts: TJsonOptions; { what the text is read with }
    S: Pointer;         { the text's reader, nil for a json }
    Cur, Last, Name, Root: Pointer;  { a json: the next node, the last read, the last name, the first }
    Ends: array of Pointer;          { a json: where each open container ends }
    NE: Integer;
    Count: Integer;     { the length of the array just opened, -1 when not known }
    FakeW0, FakeW1: Int64;  { a container read whole, as a node of its kind }
  end;
  { the members a record's json unknown keeps: their names and the text
    of their values }
  TJsonKeep = record
    N: Integer;
    Names, Vals: array of string;
  end;

  { A document being built (P207): its nodes, two words each, and its
    arena so far, a string's node keeping the place of its characters
    and a number's the place of its text until Done writes the offsets;
    the containers open, their counts and whether each holds a
    container. TJsonBuilder's, and the edits'. }
  TJsonBuild = record
    Nd: array of Int64;
    NN: Int64;
    Ar: array of Byte;
    NA: Int64;
    Open, Cnt: array of Int64;
    Cont: array of Boolean;
    Depth: Int64;
    Named: Boolean;   { in an object: a name given, its value not yet }
    Roots: Int64;     { values at the top level: one makes a document }
  end;

  { An item of an array of const as TVarRec lays it out (P124): the
    kind, then the value's words, a string's two at 8, a Quad at 16.
    JsonObject and JsonArray give their lists as these (P207). }
  TJsonVarItem = record
    VType: Int64;
    VAnsiString: string;
    VPad: Int64;
  end;

  { A document written value by value (P207): BeginObject, Name, Add,
    EndObject... Done, which reserves it once at its size and starts the
    builder again. One routine at a time: a call that finds another in
    the same builder ends the program, as a map written by two does. }
  TJsonBuilder = class(TObject)
  private
    FB: TJsonBuild;
    FBusy: Integer;
    procedure Enter;
    procedure Leave;
  public
    constructor Create;
    procedure BeginObject;
    procedure BeginArray;
    procedure EndObject;
    procedure EndArray;
    procedure Name(const S: string);
    procedure Add(const S: string); overload;
    procedure Add(V: Integer); overload;
    procedure Add(V: Double); overload;
    procedure Add(V: Boolean); overload;
    procedure Add(V: json); overload;
    procedure AddNull;
    procedure AddNumber(const Text: string);
    function Done: json;
  end;
  { A stream's bytes (P208): the next ones, '' at its end; a routine
    value, a closure as any, which may park. }
  TJsonSource = function: string;
  { Where a writer's bytes go: False stops the writer, an EJsonError of
    kind jeIO. }
  TJsonSink = function(const S: string): Boolean;
  { The kind of a stream's next token (P208): jtkEnd after its last. }
  TJsonToken = (jtkEnd, jtkNull, jtkFalse, jtkTrue, jtkNumber, jtkString, jtkBeginObject,
    jtkEndObject, jtkBeginArray, jtkEndArray);
  { An open object or array of a reader's or a writer's tokens: its
    tokens so far, and an object's names, one by one up to 64 and then
    through a table of their places too, for twins. }
  TJsonLevel = record
    Obj: Boolean;
    Count: Integer;
    NN: Integer;
    Names: array of string;
    Tab: array of Integer;
    Lit: string;        { a writer's: the last name as written, "name": }
  end;
  PJsonOut = ^TJsonOut;
  { stage 1's places, a reader's for its values' extents and parses }
  TJsonPlaces = array of UInt32;

  { A stream's values one by one (P208), from a text, a descriptor or a
    source routine: JsonRead and TryJsonRead give the next as a json, or
    into a variable of any type with a JSON form, and Peek, Next, Value
    and Skip read it a token at a time. A read that waits parks the
    routine and leaves its M free; memory is bounded by MaxValue,
    whatever the stream's size; the reader never closes its
    descriptor. Lines reads NDJSON, a value a line, and Seq an RFC 7464
    sequence; after an error in one the next read starts at the next
    line or record. One routine's at a time: a call that finds another
    running in it ends the program. }
  TJsonReader = class(TObject)
  private
    FKind: Integer;           { 0 a text, 1 a descriptor, 2 a source }
    FFd: Integer;
    FSrc: TJsonSource;
    FText: string;            { a text's bytes }
    FBuf: array of Byte;      { a descriptor's or a source's }
    FP: PByte;                { the bytes: FText's or FBuf's }
    FStart, FEnd: Integer;    { the bytes not read yet, from FP }
    FBase: Integer;           { the stream's offset of FP[0] }
    FCnt, FLine, FLineAt: Integer;  { the lines counted before FCnt, and where the last began }
    FAtEnd, FCut: Boolean;
    FOpts, FPOpts: TJsonOptions;
    FMaxValue: Integer;
    FLines, FSeq: Boolean;
    FMs: Integer;
    FBusy: Integer;
    FIdx: TJsonPlaces;        { stage 1's places, for a value's extent and its parse }
    FDepth: Integer;
    FLv: array of TJsonLevel;
    FTok: json;
    FCache: array of string;  { names, Go's stringCache }
    FLastAt, FLastLine, FLastLineAt: Integer;  { where the last value read starts, its line and the line's start }
    FErr: EJsonError;         { the error every read gives again, as Go's Decoder keeps its first }
    FSkip: Boolean;           { the rest of a line or a record too long, dropped at the next read }
    FValAt: Integer;          { the stream's offset of the value whose extent is being found, -1 none }
    FIn: Pointer;             { the parse state of a typed read's decode, kept from one value to the next }
    FPast: Integer;           { where a typed read goes on after its value, from FStart }
    procedure Enter;
    procedure Leave;
    procedure Keep(X: EJsonError; AsDoc: Boolean);
    procedure SetMaxValue(N: Integer);
    procedure SetOptions(const O: TJsonOptions);
    procedure CountTo(K: Integer);
    procedure PlaceOf(At: Integer; out ALine, ACol: Integer);
    procedure Started(S: Integer);
    procedure FailAt(At: Integer; K: TJsonErrorKind; const Reason: string);
    procedure IoFail(N: Integer);
    function More(Deadline: Integer): Boolean;
    function ByteAt(K, Deadline: Integer): Integer;
    function DueAt: Integer;
    function Closes(G: Integer; var Lv, At: Integer): Boolean;
    function NextValue(Dl: Integer; AsDoc: Boolean; out S, E, Past: Integer): Boolean;
    function ParseAt(S, E: Integer): json;
    procedure Shrink;
    function ReadDoc(out J: json): Boolean;
    function Intern(P: PByte; N: Integer): string;
    function NeedDelim: Integer;
    function TokenAt(Dl: Integer; out K: Integer): Integer;
    procedure Counted;
    procedure Descend(Obj: Boolean; At: Integer);
    function InNext(out S, E, Past: Integer): Boolean;
    function InValue(out J: json): Boolean;
  public
    constructor Create;
    function Peek: TJsonToken;
    function Next: TJsonToken;
    function Token: json;
    function AsString: string;
    function AsNumber: string;
    function Value: json;
    procedure Skip;
    function Depth: Integer;
    function Offset: Integer;
    function Line: Integer;
    function Column: Integer;
    function Path: string;
    property Lines: Boolean read FLines write FLines;
    property Seq: Boolean read FSeq write FSeq;
    property Ms: Integer read FMs write FMs;
    property MaxValue: Integer read FMaxValue write SetMaxValue;
    property Options: TJsonOptions read FOpts write SetOptions;
  end;

  { Values and tokens written to a descriptor, a sink routine or memory
    (P208): JsonWrite writes a json, or a value of any type with a JSON
    form, and BeginObject, Name, Add... write one a token at a time. A
    value at the top level is followed by a line feed (NDJSON), and in a
    sequence (Seq) preceded by RS; the bytes go out after each one, or,
    Buffered, when the buffer is three quarters full and at Flush. A
    write that waits parks the routine; one that fails, EPIPE among
    them, is an EJsonError of kind jeIO, what was not written kept. The
    writer never closes its descriptor. One routine's at a time. }
  TJsonWriter = class(TObject)
  private
    FKind: Integer;           { 0 memory, 1 a descriptor, 2 a sink }
    FFd: Integer;
    FSink: TJsonSink;
    FOut: TJsonOut;
    FTmp: TJsonOut;           { a value written for Canonical }
    FOpts: TJsonOptions;
    FSeq, FBuffered: Boolean;
    FMs: Integer;
    FBusy: Integer;
    FNamed: Boolean;          { in an object: a name written, its value not yet }
    FBase: Integer;           { the bytes given to the descriptor or the sink }
    FLv: array of TJsonLevel;
    FMarkN, FMarkDepth, FMarkCount: Integer;
    FMarkNamed: Boolean;
    procedure Enter;
    procedure Leave;
    procedure SetOptions(const O: TJsonOptions);
    procedure Mark;
    procedure Undo;
    procedure ValueStart;
    procedure ValueEnd;
    procedure Drain;
    procedure OpenLevel(Obj: Boolean);
    procedure CloseLevel(Obj: Boolean);
    procedure Scalar(Kind: Integer; const S: string; I: Integer; D: Double; J: json);
  public
    constructor Create;
    procedure BeginObject;
    procedure BeginArray;
    procedure EndObject;
    procedure EndArray;
    procedure Name(const S: string);
    procedure Add(const S: string); overload;
    procedure Add(V: Integer); overload;
    procedure Add(V: Double); overload;
    procedure Add(V: Boolean); overload;
    procedure Add(V: json); overload;
    procedure AddNull;
    procedure AddNumber(const ANumber: string);
    procedure Flush;
    function Text: string;
    function Depth: Integer;
    function Offset: Integer;
    property Seq: Boolean read FSeq write FSeq;
    property Buffered: Boolean read FBuffered write FBuffered;
    property Ms: Integer read FMs write FMs;
    property Options: TJsonOptions read FOpts write SetOptions;
  end;
{$endif}


procedure PasJsonScanStart(var S: TPasJsonScan);
function PasJsonIndexPlain(P: Pointer; N: Int64; var S: TPasJsonScan; Idx: Pointer; Off: Int64): Int64;
function PasJsonIndexCpu(P: Pointer; NBlocks: Int64; var S: TPasJsonScan; Idx: Pointer; Off: Int64): Int64;
function PasJsonIndexBase(P: Pointer; NBlocks: Int64; var S: TPasJsonScan; Idx: Pointer; Off: Int64): Int64;
function PasJsonIndexBlocks(P: Pointer; NBlocks: Int64; var S: TPasJsonScan; Idx: Pointer; Off: Int64): Int64;
function PasJsonIndex(P: Pointer; N: Int64; var S: TPasJsonScan; Idx: Pointer; Off: Int64): Int64;

function PasJsonEscIndexPlain(P: Pointer; N: Int64; Html: Boolean): Int64;
function PasJsonEscIndexCpu(P: Pointer; N: Int64; Html: Boolean): Int64;
function PasJsonEscIndexBase(P: Pointer; N: Int64; Html: Boolean): Int64;
function PasJsonEscIndex(P: Pointer; N: Int64; Html: Boolean): Int64;

{$if PASLANG_FULLVERSION >= 1001124}
function JsonIndex(J: json): TJsonIndex;
function JsonDefaults: TJsonOptions;
function JsonPretty: TJsonOptions;
function JsonCanonical: TJsonOptions;
function JsonParse(const S: string): json; overload;
function JsonParse(const S: string; const Opts: TJsonOptions): json; overload;
function TryJsonParse(const S: string; out J: json; out Err: EJsonError): Boolean; overload;
function TryJsonParse(const S: string; out J: json; out Err: EJsonError;
  const Opts: TJsonOptions): Boolean; overload;
function JsonEncode(J: json): string; overload;
function JsonEncode(J: json; const Opts: TJsonOptions): string; overload;

{ New documents from old ones (P207), the old ones unchanged: the value
  at an RFC 6901 pointer set (an object's member added when it has
  none, an array's element replaced, "-" appending) or removed; RFC
  6902's operations and RFC 7396's merge; a value as a document of its
  own, which keeps the one it came from alive no longer. }
function JsonClone(J: json): json;
function JsonSet(J: json; const Path: string; V: json): json; overload;
function JsonSet(J: json; const Path: string; const V: string): json; overload;
function JsonSet(J: json; const Path: string; V: Integer): json; overload;
function JsonSet(J: json; const Path: string; V: Double): json; overload;
function JsonSet(J: json; const Path: string; V: Boolean): json; overload;
function JsonRemove(J: json; const Path: string): json;
function JsonPatch(J, Patch: json): json;
function JsonMergePatch(J, Patch: json): json;
{ JsonObject([...]) and JsonArray([...]): the list the compiler builds }
function PasJsonOfConsts(const A: array of TJsonVarItem; Obj: Boolean): json;

{ Streams that park (P208): a reader of a text, a descriptor or a
  source routine, a writer of memory, a descriptor or a sink. JsonRead
  gives the next value, False after the last (inside a container, the
  next element or member value, False at its end); TryJsonRead gives
  its error instead of raising it; JsonWrite writes a value. Their
  forms of a variable of any type with a JSON form are the compiler's,
  through the words after them. }
function JsonReader(const Text: string): TJsonReader; overload;
function JsonReader(Fd: Integer): TJsonReader; overload;
function JsonReader(Src: TJsonSource): TJsonReader; overload;
function JsonWriter: TJsonWriter; overload;
function JsonWriter(Fd: Integer): TJsonWriter; overload;
function JsonWriter(Sink: TJsonSink): TJsonWriter; overload;
function JsonRead(R: TJsonReader; out J: json): Boolean;
function TryJsonRead(R: TJsonReader; out J: json; out Err: EJsonError): Boolean;
procedure JsonWrite(W: TJsonWriter; J: json);
function PasJsonReadBegin(R: TJsonReader; var D: TJsonIn): Boolean;
procedure PasJsonReadFail(R: TJsonReader; E: EJsonError);
procedure PasJsonReadEnd(R: TJsonReader);
function PasJsonWriteBegin(W: TJsonWriter): PJsonOut;
procedure PasJsonWriteEnd(W: TJsonWriter);
procedure PasJsonWriteUndo(W: TJsonWriter);

{ The words the compiler writes for j['k'], j[i], 'k' in j, TryGet,
  Length, =, Write and for ... in (P203). }
function PasJsonGet(J: json; const K: string): json;
function PasJsonItem(J: json; I: Integer): json;
function PasJsonHas(J: json; const K: string): Boolean;
function PasJsonTryGet(J: json; const K: string; out V: json): Boolean;
