{ The parser that reads a byte at a time, without the index (Plain):
  the tests hold the other to it, document for document (P203). Nil
  and Err on an error, as TryJsonParse. }
function PasJsonParsePlain(const S: string; const Opts: TJsonOptions; out Err: EJsonError): json;
{ The bytes of the document J is the root of, its header to the end of
  its arena: two parses of a text give the same. }
function PasJsonImage(J: json): string;

{ The words of the encoders the compiler writes (P205). A member is
  PasJsonOutName with its name as written, "name":, and its value; an
  element PasJsonOutItem and its value; Quoted writes a number inside a
  string (json quoted). Each raises EJsonError with the JSON Pointer of
  the value it could not write: a string that is not UTF-8 or a
  noncharacter (jeEncoding), NaN, an infinity, a Char past 127, a value
  no member of its enumeration, a TDateTime past year 9999 (jeRange),
  a level past MaxDepth (jeDepth). }
procedure PasJsonOutInit(var W: TJsonOut; const Opts: TJsonOptions; Hint: Integer);
function PasJsonOutText(var W: TJsonOut; const Opts: TJsonOptions): string;
procedure PasJsonOutOpen(var W: TJsonOut; Obj: Boolean);
