{ The words of the decoders the compiler writes (P206, P280): each
  reads the next value of the cursor, or the name just read, into the
  type T names, a JSON null as its zero, or raises EJsonError with the
  JSON Pointer of the value and, from text, the line, the column and the
  byte it starts at: jeType for a kind or a form the type does not take,
  jeRange past its range, jeMissing and jeUnknown for a member,
  jeDuplicate for a member of a set given twice, and a parse's errors
  for the text, the first in its order. }
